    <section class="work wrap section" id="work" aria-labelledby="work-title">
      <div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">01 / The work</p><h2 id="work-title">Complexity is a given.<br><em>Confusion is optional.</em></h2><p>Three connected fields. One purpose: better decisions under real constraints.</p></div>
      <div class="work-rows">
        <article class="work-row"><span class="row-number mono">01</span><div><h3>Applied AI integration</h3><p>Put models to work where they make a difference. Map the workflow, evaluate the options, and build around useful outcomes.</p><ul class="tags" aria-label="Applied AI themes"><li>Workflow discovery</li><li>Model evaluation</li><li>Governance</li></ul></div><span class="row-symbol" aria-hidden="true">⌘</span></article>
        <article class="work-row"><span class="row-number mono">02</span><div><h3>Strategic &amp; geopolitical risk</h3><p>Read the context around the technology. Examine institutions, incentives, and dependencies before committing to a direction.</p><ul class="tags" aria-label="Strategy themes"><li>Decision support</li><li>Technology risk</li><li>Scenario analysis</li></ul></div><span class="row-symbol" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></article>
        <article class="work-row"><span class="row-number mono">03</span><div><h3>Cognitive Labs</h3><p>Investigate how models behave and how people work with them. Careful experiments, adversarial questions, and explicit uncertainty.</p><ul class="tags" aria-label="Research themes"><li>Model behavior</li><li>Adversarial prompting</li><li>Human-AI resilience</li></ul></div><span class="row-symbol" aria-hidden="true">◎</span></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="desk-section" id="field-desk" aria-labelledby="desk-title"><div class="wrap">
      <div class="desk-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / The field desk</p><h2 id="desk-title">Better questions.<br><em>Stronger decisions.</em></h2></div><p>A small demonstration of how we think.<br>Select a question. Inspect the brief behind it.</p></div>
      <div class="desk">
        <div class="desk-input"><div class="desk-label mono">THE STARTING QUESTION</div><div class="scenario-buttons" role="group" aria-label="Example questions"><button type="button" data-scenario="ai" aria-pressed="true">“Where should we use AI?” <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button><button type="button" data-scenario="risk" aria-pressed="false">“What are we missing?” <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button><button type="button" data-scenario="labs" aria-pressed="false">“Can we trust this model?” <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button></div><div class="desk-note"><span class="tiny-cross" aria-hidden="true">+</span><p>A good brief exposes assumptions before they become decisions.</p></div></div>
        <div class="desk-output"><div class="output-head"><span class="desk-label mono">THE WORKING BRIEF</span><button class="copy-button" type="button" id="copy-brief">Copy brief <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button></div><div id="brief" aria-live="polite"><h3>Start with the work, then choose the model.</h3><dl><div><dt>Frame</dt><dd>Choose one repeatable workflow and define the outcome worth improving.</dd></div><div><dt>Investigate</dt><dd>Compare the current process, a simpler automation, and an AI-assisted approach on the same representative tasks.</dd></div><div><dt>Challenge</dt><dd>Identify failure costs, sensitive information, and the points that require human review.</dd></div><div><dt>Decide</dt><dd>Run a bounded pilot. Continue only if quality, time saved, and operating costs justify it.</dd></div></dl></div><p class="desk-disclosure">Illustrative briefs, prepared in advance. No model calls or input collection.</p><span id="copy-status" role="status"></span></div>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="approach wrap section" id="approach" aria-labelledby="approach-title"><div class="approach-copy"><p class="eyebrow">03 / The approach</p><h2 id="approach-title">Small surface area.<br><em>High signal.</em></h2><p>Independent B2B advisory, scoped to the problem. Practical work that respects operational and human constraints.</p><a class="text-link" href="mailto:advisory@gillist.com">Discuss an engagement <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div class="principles"><div><span class="mono">01</span><h3>Discretion first.</h3><p>Client matters stay confidential by default.</p></div><div><span class="mono">02</span><h3>Show the reasoning.</h3><p>Distinguish evidence, interpretation, and what remains unknown.</p></div><div><span class="mono">03</span><h3>Make it useful.</h3><p>Recommendations should lead to a concrete action or a testable decision.</p></div><div><span class="mono">04</span><h3>Build for the long horizon.</h3><p>Develop durable capability with room to adapt as conditions change.</p></div></div></section>

